EFK vs Prometheus

| Feature          | Prometheus                 | EFK                             |
| ---------------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Collects         | Metrics                    | Logs                            |
| Example          | CPU, Memory, Request Count | INFO, WARN, ERROR, Exceptions   |
| Storage          | Time-series database       | Elasticsearch                   |
| Visualization    | Grafana                    | Kibana                          |
| Alerts           | Yes (Alertmanager)         | Via log queries or integrations |
| Typical Question | "Is CPU high?"             | "Why did the application fail?" |


Example Incident:
A user reports that login isn't working.

Prometheus shows:

CPU: Normal
Memory: Normal
Pods: Healthy

Metrics alone don't reveal the cause.

In Kibana, you search for ERROR and find:

ORA-01017: invalid username/password

The logs identify the root cause.


