Where this fits into your observability stack

Given what you've already built:

Prometheus → Collects metrics (CPU, memory, request counts, JVM metrics).
Grafana → Visualizes those metrics.
Alertmanager → Sends alerts based on metric rules.
EFK → Centralizes and searches application and Kubernetes logs.
Jaeger (optional next step) → Traces requests across services.

Together, these provide the three main pillars of observability:

Metrics – "What is happening?"
Logs – "Why did it happen?"
Traces – "Where did it happen across services?"
